{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS PROBLEMATIC BECAUSE IT OVERSIMPLIFIES THE COMPLEXITY OF DEALING WITH UNJUST LAWS. IT FAILS TO PROVIDE CONTEXT OR GUIDANCE ON HOW TO DETERMINE WHETHER A LAW IS BAD, LEAVING THE READER WITHOUT A CLEAR UNDERSTANDING OF HOW TO APPLY THIS PRINCIPLE IN PRACTICE. FURTHERMORE, IT DOES NOT CONSIDER THE POTENTIAL CONSEQUENCES OF DISREGARDING A LAW, EVEN IF IT IS PERCEIVED AS BAD.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nMOREOVER, THE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" CAN BE SEEN AS PROMOTING A FORM OF LEGAL NIHILISM, WHERE INDIVIDUALS PICK AND CHOOSE WHICH LAWS TO FOLLOW BASED ON PERSONAL OPINION RATHER THAN THE RULE OF LAW. THIS APPROACH CAN LEAD TO CHAOS AND UNDERMINES THE SOCIAL CONTRACT, AS IT IGNORES THE ESTABLISHED PROCESSES FOR CHALLENGING AND CHANGING LAWS. A MORE CONSTRUCTIVE APPROACH MIGHT INVOLVE ENGAGING WITH THE LEGAL SYSTEM TO REFORM OR REPEAL BAD LAWS, RATHER THAN SIMPLY DISREGARDING THEM.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.003181398380547762}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.0001438752660760656}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -2.7418097943154862e-06}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " LAW", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " BAD", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " YOU", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " SHOULD", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " NOT", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " FOLLOW", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " IT", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": -0.0498855635